+# The Daily Grind
+
+Coffee shop site with passwordless accounts, discoverable passkey sign-in, passkey management, and action-specific reauthentication.
+
+## Run
+
+Requires Node.js 24+ and pnpm.
+
+```sh
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm start
+```
+
+Open `http://localhost:11222`. Create an account from **My Account → Create an account**. Registration uses a unique username, not an email address; no email verification or password recovery is implied. A compatible password manager, screen lock, phone, or discoverable security key is required. Passkeys are created and verified using native WebAuthn APIs and SimpleWebAuthn on the server.
+
+The account panel is also available at `/account`. Users can add and rename passkeys, remove passkeys after verification, edit their display name, verify their identity, and sign out. Adding a passkey, removing one, or changing the account name requires verification with an existing passkey. Keep a backup passkey: the final passkey cannot be removed, and there is no insecure account recovery bypass.
+
+## Deployment
+
+```sh
+NODE_ENV=production ORIGIN=https://coffee.example.com PORT=11222 pnpm start
+```
+
+Set `ORIGIN` to the exact externally visible HTTPS origin, with no trailing slash or path. The relying party ID is its hostname. Deploy behind an HTTPS reverse proxy and retain the same domain: passkeys are scoped to that domain. In development only, an omitted `ORIGIN` uses the request host and protocol to support localhost and HTTPS preview hosts.
+
+Accounts, public keys, signature counters, hashed session tokens, and pending challenges are persisted in SQLite at `./data/daily-grind.sqlite`. Set `DATABASE_PATH` to change it. Mount this directory on persistent storage and back it up. This server requires a Node process and is not a static-only deployment. The start command builds the client bundle; install development dependencies during build/start. `pnpm build` can also be run separately and `node server.js` starts an already-built deployment.
+
+Sessions expire after 24 hours, use HttpOnly/SameSite=Strict cookies (Secure on HTTPS), and rotate on sign-in and sign-out. Challenges expire after five minutes and are single use and session bound. Reauthentication grants expire after two minutes and are single use and action bound. User verification is required on both registration and authentication. Removal revokes other account sessions. Same-origin mutation checks, request limits, a restrictive content security policy, and credential ownership checks are enforced server-side.
+
+Native WebAuthn JSON serialization and client capabilities use `webauthn-polyfills` for older compatible browsers. Conditional autofill and password-manager Signal APIs are feature detected. Missing Signal APIs never prevent account actions. Security keys remain usable even when a platform authenticator is absent.
+
+## Automated checks
+
+```sh
+pnpm test
+```
+
+Server integration tests generate real P-256 credentials and signatures and exercise SimpleWebAuthn verification without a browser. They cover registration, authentication, challenge reuse/expiry, malicious origins, missing user verification, invalid signatures, session isolation, account ownership, management, reauthentication scopes, final-passkey protection, and persistence. Client tests exercise account UI flows in an automated DOM environment. No manual browser checks are required.
+
+Provider names and icons in `providers.json` are a small snapshot of the [Passkey Developer AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids). Unrecognized or zero AAGUIDs show a generic icon and provider name. AAGUIDs are display hints only and never authorize access.
